# An allowlist for api/Dockerfile: only the files the API image needs are sent to the build, so secrets such as
# .env and .env.api, local environments, and Git history can never end up in an image. BuildKit reads this file
# instead of the root .dockerignore because it sits next to the Dockerfile with the same name.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!.python-version
!README.md
# Hatch builds the project's package from pipelines/; the API reads its version from that package's metadata.
!pipelines/
!api/
**/__pycache__
api/Dockerfile
api/Dockerfile.dockerignore
api/app.yaml
